**Clarify requirements.** Where does data come from (any REST endpoint, e.g. a list of image URLs)? Should there be prev/next buttons and dots? Does the timer reset on manual navigation? Start with the core, then extend.

**State.** `items` (fetched), `loading`, `error`, `index`, `playing` (default true).

**Fetch.** In a `useEffect` with `[]` deps, call `fetch`, check `res.ok`, set items; guard against unmount with an `AbortController` (abort in cleanup).

**Auto-advance.** One effect keyed on `playing`, `items.length` and `index`:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!playing || items.length === 0) return;
  const id = setTimeout(() => setIndex(i => (i + 1) % items.length), 5000);
  return () => clearTimeout(id);
}, [playing, index, items.length]);
```
Using `setTimeout` keyed on `index` means any manual navigation automatically restarts the 5 s countdown, and the cleanup prevents leaks and duplicate timers. The functional update `i => ...` avoids stale closures. `setInterval` also works if you keep it in a ref and clean it up.

**Render.** Show the current item, prev/next buttons, a dot indicator, and a Pause/Play `<button>` that toggles `playing` (label via state, `aria-label`). Show a spinner while loading and a message on error or empty data.

**Extras if time permits:** pause on hover/focus, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, preload the next image, keyboard arrows, `aria-live="polite"` on the slide, and slide transition with CSS.

**Common mistakes:** leaving the interval running after unmount; creating a new interval on every render; mutating state directly; using modulo with negative index for 'prev' (use `(i - 1 + n) % n`); not handling empty arrays.
